In the exhibition people speak only quietly.
I walk slowly through the gallery.
Many old landscape paintings of Berlin hang here.
Finally, I stop in front of two pictures.
They hang directly next to each other and show the same lake.
I compare the two artworks in my head.
This picture here has very warm and bright colors.
That picture next to it is rather dark and cold.
I decide quickly: I like this picture much more than that picture!
I immediately take my phone out of my pocket.
I take a quick photo of the bright artwork.
Then I send it to Nele, my colleague from the company.
I type a short message to her.
"Do you remember?"
"We talked about art a few weeks ago."
"This picture here immediately reminds me of our conversation."
Nele normally never answers on Sundays, but that is completely fine.
I put the phone away again and look at the painting for another moment.
